sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: docs/reference/feature-flow.md section 6, one Swamp workflow per Gateway release, manual or automatic.
  %% Container releases keep the former live stopped as old for rollback; migrations are expand-only. docs/reference/gateway-recovery.md#release-as-a-swamp-run.
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: gateway:release:deploy
  %% kind: gateway.release
  %% behavior name: gateway-release-<step>-209 (fixed)
  autonumber
  %% lane TR icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane AC icon=workflow pill=child tone=green
  %% lane GN icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant TR as CLI<br/>orbit · MCP
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant AC as Activate run<br/>child · new commit
  participant GN as Gateway Node<br/>Node 14
  alt Reload serving workflows
    TR->>GW: gateway:release:deploy<br/>--reconcile · exact serving SHA
    GW->>SW: Start reconciliation
    SW->>GN: Check the serving release
    SW->>SW: Reload serving workflows
    SW->>GN: Verify the serving release
    SW->>GN: Release the serving<br/>generation
    SW-->>GW: Reconciled release record
  else Deploy a release
  TR->>GW: gateway:release:deploy<br/>full sha
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit gateway:release:deploy <full sha>`; the automatic tick admits the newest green commit the same way
  Note over GW: Admit the release<br/>verify agent pin · web build
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the full commit; no other release queued or running
  %%> - the agent pin passes its Sigstore check; CI published the commit's web build
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a running release record; the pin, artifact, Horizon unit and SSH targets frozen as inputs
  GW->>SW: Start release workflow<br/>shared or legacy selection
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Container releases select production-release. The host release path selects operation-gateway-release.
  %%> - At run start, the Gateway writes the scoped read token to the vault.
  GW-->>TR: 202 Accepted<br/>running release record
  opt Container release
    Note over SW: Check release ownership
  end
  SW->>GN: Fetch the commit<br/>shared repository
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - fetches the commit with the read token when the shared repository lacks it; the token reaches git only in its environment
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for review:
  %%> - the fetch is its own step, so that the build runs its script from the commit being released, not from the live release
  SW->>GN: Build the release<br/>wake and update preparation
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - refuses a commit that does not descend from the current release on a container Gateway
  %%> - on a container Gateway, checks the target commit's activation workflow and recovery script before waking it or loading its Swamp workflows
  %%> - checks out the exact commit and installs dependencies in the preparation container; its workers and scheduler stay disabled
  %%> - a retry after an incomplete build starts from a clean checkout and discards partial build output
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - the host PHP-FPM build checks disk space for the build and database copy
  SW->>GN: Install the web build<br/>artifact · digest · rename
  alt Container release
    SW->>GN: Clone the prepared release<br/>seal · promote preparation
    SW->>GN: Sleep preparation<br/>before migration
  else Host PHP-FPM release
    SW->>GN: Snapshot the database<br/>VACUUM INTO
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - keeps the newest two snapshots and any snapshot named by a pause
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - refuses before the copy when it would breach the disk floor
  end
  SW->>GN: Migrate<br/>artisan migrate --isolated=1
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the container candidate applies pending migrations to the shared production database
  %%> - prints the end of the migration's output and its exit code; a failed exec would keep no output
  Note over SW: Check the migration<br/>assert the exit code
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - a failed container migration leaves the current release serving
  %%> - the record's message ends with the migration's output
  opt Host PHP-FPM release
    SW->>GN: Wait for active Operations<br/>before loading workflows
  end
    SW->>GN: Check the candidate<br/>FrankenPHP · health · commit
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - discard the candidate; live keeps serving and the Swamp load does not start
    Note over SW: Load Swamp on Node 209<br/>operation-gateway-swamp-load
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the load child checks the target on the Gateway Node before updating the checkout, grants and loaded workflows
    Note over SW: Hand over the release<br/>run the selected child
    opt the Gateway serves through host PHP-FPM
      AC->>GN: Drain Horizon<br/>systemctl stop · SIGTERM only
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - waits for the unit's whole control group to empty, up to the drain limit
      %%> On failure:
      %%> - the run fails with `gateway.release_horizon_unit_stale` for a unit without the stop policy, or `gateway.release_horizon_not_drained` when the unit did not stop in time
    end
    AC->>GN: Switch the release<br/>commit · publish upstream
    par Public readiness
      AC->>GN: Verify the Gateway<br/>health and serving SHA
      %%> - reads `/up` and the status version with sudo: the pinned root CA sits in the private certificate folder, `root:caddy 0750`
    and Container workers
      AC->>GN: Start Horizon<br/>on the selected release
    end
    opt Container Gateway
      AC->>GN: Quiesce the previous live<br/>drain HTTP and Horizon
      AC->>GN: Wait for queued responses<br/>Ansible retries · bounded
      AC->>GN: Retire the previous live<br/>stop it as old
      AC->>GN: Recreate preparation<br/>clone · promote
      AC->>GN: Record eligible versions<br/>file cleanup Tasks
    end
    opt Failed host PHP-FPM check
      AC->>GN: Switch back<br/>restore host release
    end
    AC->>GN: Resume document cleanup
    alt every step succeeded
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
      Note over GW: Record verified<br/>fleet rollout follows
      %%> - the cleanup step files Tasks for earlier releases' versions once a later verified release has deleted the stopped old that held the earlier code
      %%> Next:
      %%> - the Gateway queues the existing fleet admission job; it follows each Node’s delivery and scoped role converge in order
      %%> - when enabled, nested-fleet refresh follows the first transition to `current`; with fleet rollout disabled it follows verification
    else a step before Migrate fails
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
      Note over GW: Mark failed<br/>nothing changed · rerun safe
    else the host switched back
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
      Note over GW: Record switched back<br/>alert · next commit releases
    else a container check fails
      SW--xGW: Report failed phase
      Note over GW: Roll back to old<br/>or deploy a fix
    else a host migration or later step fails
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
      Note over GW: Pause automatic releases<br/>failed step · alert
    end
  SW->>GN: Release unused candidate<br/>after handover or failure
  %%> Returns a candidate of this Operation that never served to the preparation slot. The selected release, old and a pending drain remain protected.
  end
